  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through Monday)\nIssued at 1112 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nA strong area of high pressure will remain just west of the area \nWednesday through Friday. This will keep temperatures hot, with \nhighs in the mid 90s to low 100s each day. Both Wednesday and\nThursday have a good chance of Heat Advisory issuance for at least\nportions of the area. A surface cold front will stall out near \nthe OK- KS border late Wednesday into Thursday, with a few showers\nand storms forming near it. Considering the hot surface \ntemperatures and somewhat lower than typical dew points, any \nstorms will have the potential to be wind producers. Overall \ncoverage will be quite isolated.\n\nA better chance of rain arrives later Thursday into Friday as a \nshortwave trough passes through, with ensembles showing a good \nchance of showers and storms. This would be the best and only chance \nfor meaningful rain for most locations. Some guidance suggests a few \nhigh terrain showers or storms could linger into Saturday over \nArkansas, but otherwise hot and dry weather will then extend through \nthe weekend and into early next week.",
